{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "turn", "session": {"id": "s-fdb50a531783", "start_time": "2026-09-22T10:38:18.340Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 0, "timestamp": "2026-09-22T10:38:25.153Z", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5", "model_version": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "tokens_in": 1522, "tokens_out": 96, "latency": 6.7886, "finish_reason": "tool_use"}, "content": {"prompt_text": "A policyholder has complained about how long their claim is taking. What does the complaints procedure require me to do, and in what timescales?", "prompt_hash": "sha256:83fcef418a0b95490334371d7b1c56892dccb6dfc20e9db779593fb21b917813", "response_text": "I'll search for information about the complaints procedure for you.", "response_hash": "sha256:c6761cbb3bfca2c6c9b5a8ca130405d5ae0163f309accef82d8a263b0a86de15", "system_prompt_version": "sp-0.2.0", "redaction_applied": false}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "turn", "session": {"id": "s-fdb50a531783", "start_time": "2026-09-22T10:38:18.340Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 1, "timestamp": "2026-09-22T10:38:25.413Z", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5", "model_version": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "tokens_in": 9296, "tokens_out": 277, "latency": 0.2592, "finish_reason": "end_turn"}, "content": {"prompt_text": "A policyholder has complained about how long their claim is taking. What does the complaints procedure require me to do, and in what timescales?", "prompt_hash": "sha256:83fcef418a0b95490334371d7b1c56892dccb6dfc20e9db779593fb21b917813", "response_text": "Based on the complaints procedure, here's what you must do:\n\n**Recording:**\n- Log the complaint on the complaints system on the day it is received, including the date, how it arrived, what the complaint is about in the complainant's own words, and your name. (prc-complaints-004)\n\n**Timescales:**\n\n- **By close of the next working day:** Acknowledge in writing, giving the name of the person who will handle the complaint.\n\n- **By day three:** If the complaint can be resolved to the complainant's satisfaction, send a summary resolution communication.\n\n- **By week four:** If it is not resolved, write to explain why not and when a final response is expected.\n\n- **By week eight:** Send the final response, or explain why one cannot yet be given and tell the complainant of their right to escalate (the procedure was cut off in the available text, but this is the standard FCA deadline). (prc-complaints-004)\n\nThe key point is that silence is damaging—the guidance on subsidence claims specifically notes that \"silence during a monitoring period is the single largest source of complaints on this class\", so keeping the complainant informed of progress (or lack thereof) is essential. (prc-subsidence-005)", "response_hash": "sha256:4f59dec63669432889712808228de483db90be401cf1a8e76a07e07cba89e91f", "system_prompt_version": "sp-0.2.0", "redaction_applied": false}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
